huz|v|To press, force, or drive, particularly in filling, or in thrusting one thing into another; to stuff; to crowd; to fill to superfluity; as, to cram anything into a basket; to cram a room with people. ; To fill with food to satiety; to stuff. ; To put hastily through an extensive course of memorizing or study, as in preparation for an examination; as, a pupil is crammed by his tutor. ; To eat greedily, and to satiety; to stuff. ; To make crude preparation for a special occasion, as an examination, by a hasty and extensive course of memorizing or study.	o:s56,37,2~s56,37,2	s:254e,18,3~254e,18,3	D:29qk,52,15~29qk,52,15
