i7p|n|Qualified to criticise, or pass judgment upon, literary or artistic productions. ; Pertaining to criticism or the critic's art; of the nature of a criticism; accurate; as, critical knowledge; a critical dissertation. ; Inclined to make nice distinctions, or to exercise careful judgment and selection; exact; nicely judicious. ; Inclined to criticise or find fault; fastidious; captious; censorious; exacting. ; Characterized by thoroughness and a reference to principles, as becomes a critic; as, a critical analysis of a subject. ; Pertaining to, or indicating, a crisis, turning point, or specially important juncture; important as regards consequences; hence, of doubtful issue; attended with risk; dangerous; as, the critical stage of a fever; a critical situation.	a:bcj,67,3;1fc2,16,53;22gw,3,58~22gw,3,58;1fc2,16,53;bcj,67,3	v:guw,33,3;lcc,23,5;kip,23,3;gje,16,3;27u0,12,5~lcc,23,5;27u0,12,5;guw,33,3;gje,16,3;kip,23,3	V:fa5,64,8;p30,28,4;14ty,21,32;27pl,19,7~14ty,21,32;fa5,64,8;27pl,19,7;p30,28,4	n:1xmp,43,7;cy9,32,4;1aj9,22,3;1zax,12,3~1xmp,43,7;cy9,32,4;1zax,12,3;1aj9,22,3	N:4gm,94,18;1ttr,91,4;28wa,86,7;1ujt,56,6;158z,45,3;13f5,42,12;35u,39,30;5b7,39,12;1wu4,36,14;s8r,36,3;s28,33,9;5fc,33,6;nal,31,4;5uy,28,3;1zax,26,8~35u,39,30;rjn,24,18;4gm,94,18;28w4,11,16;2784,8,14;1wu4,36,14;5b7,39,12;13f5,42,12;s28,33,9;1w5g,18,9;mk8,19,9;1zax,26,8;28wa,86,7;2823,21,6;1ujt,56,6
